    "result": "Excellent! All 28 tests across all 8 test files are now passing. Here's a summary of the fixes:\n\n## Issues Fixed\n\n1. **Governance test - \"flags schema violations with descriptive errors\"**\n   - **Problem**: The test was trying to import `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export from `src/finetune/index.js`, but it wasn't being exported.\n   - **Fix**: Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS` in `index.js` (alongside the existing default export for backward compatibility).\n\n2. **Evaluation test - \"runs default evaluations\"**\n   - **Problem**: The `toxicityMetric` function expected a `bannedTerms` parameter, but `runEvaluations` was calling all metrics with `(outputs, references)`. The references were being incorrectly used as banned terms, causing the toxicity score to be 0 instead of 1.\n   - **Fix**: Changed the `toxicityMetric` signature to accept `references` as the second parameter (matching the interface expected by `runEvaluations`) and updated the function to always use the default banned terms instead of the parameter value.\n\nAll public exports remain intact and fully functional.",
